# C++ Strings Cheatsheet

## Char ↔ Int
```cpp
// char -> int
int d  = c - '0';    // digit char to int:  '7' -> 7
int i  = c - 'a';    // lowercase to index: 'a'->0 ... 'z'->25
int i  = c - 'A';    // uppercase to index: 'A'->0 ... 'Z'->25

// int -> char
char c = d + '0';    // digit int to char:  7 -> '7'
char c = i + 'a';    // index to lowercase: 0->'a' ... 25->'z'
char c = i + 'A';    // index to uppercase: 0->'A' ... 25->'Z'
```

## String ↔ Int
```cpp
int n    = stoi(s);          // "123" -> 123 (handles sign, skips spaces)
string s = to_string(n);     // 123 -> "123"
```

## Char checks (`<cctype>`)
```cpp
isalpha(c)   isdigit(c)   isalnum(c)   isspace(c)
islower(c)   isupper(c)
tolower(c)   toupper(c)   // return new value, don't modify in place
```

## Overflow guard (check BEFORE *10)
```cpp
// 7 and 8 = last digit of INT_MAX (...647) and INT_MIN (...648)
if (res > INT_MAX/10 || (res == INT_MAX/10 && d > 7)) // pos overflow
if (res < INT_MIN/10 || (res == INT_MIN/10 && d < -8)) // neg overflow
res = res * 10 + d;
```

## Substring
```cpp
// substr: takes INDICES (len = how many chars, not end index)
s.substr(2, 3)       // 3 chars starting at index 2
s.substr(2)          // index 2 to end

// iterators: use the string CONSTRUCTOR, not substr
string(s.begin(), s.begin() + 3)   // first 3 chars
string(s.begin() + 2, s.end())     // index 2 to end
```

## Access & iterate
```cpp
s[i]   s.size()   s.empty()
s.front()   // first char, same as s[0]
s.back()    // last char,  same as s[s.size()-1]

for (char c : s)        // by value
for (char& c : s)       // by reference (modify)
int l = 0, r = s.size()-1;   // two pointers
```

## Common ops
```cpp
s += c;            s.push_back(c);     s.pop_back();
s.find("ab")       // index or string::npos
reverse(s.begin(), s.end());   // <algorithm>
```


'5' - '0' = 5     (char → int)
'0' + 5 = '5'     (int → char)
